    {
      "id": "about",
      "index": "05",
      "label": "about abaddion / contact",
      "route": "/about",
      "title": "about",
      "byline": "Barbora Jenšík — Barush",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The meeting point of art, abstraction and technology has always fascinated me. Maybe that's why I'm so in love with glitch. Everything is built on chaos anyway. And on paradox.",
        "My art expresses the things I love. I see it as technical design: a mix of polaroid photography, data and lines, math and the universe. It's hard to explain. It's a world I carry in my head.",
        "Twenty years in technical recruitment left me with an endless thirst for innovation, improvement and effectiveness. I honor that knowledge by building products I believe will make the professional world better.",
        "Building a team should start with the employer brand. There is a unique connection between the right talent and the right company, and today's hiring process makes it almost invisible. There is so much data out there. Used well, AI can help us connect the dots faster and more effectively, without drowning in it."
      ],
      "ctaLinks": [
        {
          "lead": "If you like my art, some of it is for sale.",
          "href": "/canvas",
          "label": "canvas"
        },
        {
          "lead": "If you feel you've tried everything and hiring is still slow, let me evaluate your employer brand and build it for you.",
          "href": "/career-pages",
          "label": "career pages"
        }
      ],
      "closingLine": "Otherwise, enjoy the glitch.",
